      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's understandable that you're worried about hospital visits; however, the current high blood sugar is a life-threatening condition that needs immediate medical attention. Delaying by attempting to sober them up at home with insulin could lead to serious complications, such as diabetic ketoacidosis, which can be more dangerous than the hospital stay.\n\nYour priority should be stabilizing their condition as quickly and safely as possible. The healthcare professionals can check their glucose levels, ketones, hydration, and other vitals, and they will have the necessary equipment to intervene effectively. Keep them hydrated with water, but this is not a substitute for medical care.\n\nContact your local emergency services alone. Make sure they're aware of the situation and the urgency while also explaining the potential consequences of delaying treatment. They may be able to guide you on the next steps to take and help prevent the healthcare cost by negating hospital bills that may arise from complications.",
